---
description: Never commit secrets; keep .env.local and API keys out of git
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets

- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, `.cursor/.env.deploy`, or any file matching `.env*`. Use `.env.example` for placeholders only.
- Never write real API keys, tokens, or passwords into source, rules, skills, or docs.
- User API keys live in Prisma `ApiKey` (hashed/secret fields). Do not log `secret`, `passwordHash`, or raw provider keys.
- Skill caches that might hold secrets stay gitignored (`.cursor/**/.env*`, skill `node_modules`, `.sync-manifest.json`).
- If a command needs credentials, read them from the environment. Do not overwrite `.env.local`.
